WEBVTT

00:04.560 --> 00:05.310
Sensei...

00:06.490 --> 00:07.190
What is it?

00:10.040 --> 00:12.500
There's something I want to ask you.

01:40.990 --> 01:44.240
<b>Staff 
Office</b>

01:41.540 --> 01:45.740
Why did you choose to have four tubas?

01:47.390 --> 01:53.800
Because if we're aspiring to the Nationals, 
we need to strengthen the bass.

01:53.800 --> 01:55.950
I understand that.

01:55.950 --> 01:56.460
It's just...

01:58.900 --> 01:59.790
Well...

02:00.260 --> 02:05.070
I'm trying to figure out what 
your musical goals are.

02:06.330 --> 02:07.380
I see.

02:08.060 --> 02:11.780
That's a very difficult question to answer.

02:11.780 --> 02:14.170
If I had to answer,

02:14.170 --> 02:19.750
I'd say I'm aiming for music that would 
yield results for everyone's improvement.

02:19.750 --> 02:23.320
So music specifically 
tailored for competitions?

02:23.700 --> 02:33.170
I hear that phrase often, but personally, 
I'm not sure if such music even exists.

02:33.500 --> 02:34.370
Then...

02:35.240 --> 02:39.630
The club has decided that winning 
gold in the Nationals is your goal.

02:40.520 --> 02:45.590
What kind of changes should 
I bring to the Prefecturals?

02:46.050 --> 02:48.190
What kind of performance should we give?

02:49.190 --> 02:51.600
That's all I'm thinking about right now.

02:53.330 --> 02:56.330
I'm sorry for the rude comment.

02:58.350 --> 02:59.340
<i>He's right.</i>

02:59.780 --> 03:04.540
<i>We were the ones who said we 
wanted gold in the Nationals.</i>

03:05.350 --> 03:06.800
Please put your hand out.

03:10.520 --> 03:13.050
The vice president gave it to me.

03:13.050 --> 03:15.250
Don't tell the other members.

03:15.250 --> 03:17.070
Okay.

03:18.110 --> 03:21.760
<i>"Please explain why you chose 
Kuroe-san for the soli part."</i>

03:22.770 --> 03:27.640
<i>I held back the question 
I most wanted to ask.</i>

03:26.810 --> 03:30.730
<b>Episode 10</b>

03:26.810 --> 03:30.730
<b>Expressing Arpeggios</b>

03:39.300 --> 03:43.860
Okay, the competition members will 
be having ensemble rehearsal now.

03:43.860 --> 03:49.360
Um, are we going to be practicing 
like this going forward?

03:49.360 --> 03:52.360
The members change every 
time we have an audition.

03:52.360 --> 03:56.010
I don't know if that really 
helps us play better.

03:56.920 --> 03:58.780
We're in the middle of practice.

03:58.780 --> 04:00.330
Let's talk about it later.

04:00.690 --> 04:02.450
I promise I'll hear you out.

04:03.650 --> 04:04.630
Of course.

04:04.630 --> 04:07.960
Please don't blame your 
discontent on the auditions.

04:08.310 --> 04:10.720
We all knew what we were getting into.

04:11.000 --> 04:14.230
I'm not trying to complain.

04:14.230 --> 04:18.850
And it was Taki-sensei who decided we would 
be holding auditions for each competition.

04:18.850 --> 04:21.900
It wasn't Taki-sensei who decided that.

04:21.900 --> 04:23.060
Really?

04:26.570 --> 04:28.650
It was the executives who proposed it.

04:28.650 --> 04:31.790
Although Taki-sensei was the one 
who made the final decision.

04:31.790 --> 04:36.410
Then if we said we wanted to go back 
to how we were doing it before...

04:36.410 --> 04:38.300
How do you expect us to do that now?

04:38.300 --> 04:42.330
Th-The executive team understands that 
there are people who feel that way.

04:42.330 --> 04:45.960
But we already decided that this is 
how we would do things this year.

04:45.960 --> 04:47.210
It'll have to be next year...

04:47.210 --> 04:50.110
So you mean we have to give up on this year?

04:50.860 --> 04:53.210
No one said that.

04:53.210 --> 04:56.640
Taki-sensei determined that 
this was the for the best.

04:56.640 --> 04:59.520
We believe in him and continue 
to perform accordingly.

04:59.520 --> 05:00.920
Still, though...

05:01.360 --> 05:04.290
Do something about the 
bad vibes in the club.

05:04.290 --> 05:07.600
It's been really nasty ever since camp.

05:07.600 --> 05:09.450
Don't you feel it yourself?

05:09.780 --> 05:12.720
You got switched off the 
soli out of nowhere.

05:13.280 --> 05:16.770
Isn't that kind of thing pretty...

05:21.560 --> 05:23.040
What's the matter?

05:23.040 --> 05:25.430
We don't have time to be resting.

05:25.430 --> 05:26.820
R-Right.

05:27.850 --> 05:28.830
All rise!

05:34.250 --> 05:36.470
Are you saying it's my fault?!

05:36.470 --> 05:40.100
This is all because you go around being 
a people pleaser of a vice president!

05:40.100 --> 05:42.700
That has nothing to do with this!

05:42.700 --> 05:44.650
The president's trying to calm things down.

05:44.650 --> 05:48.010
You don't need to react 
to everything people say!

05:48.010 --> 05:50.060
It's even worse that we just let it slide.

05:50.060 --> 05:53.190
We'd be admitting to being 
wrong by not addressing it.

05:53.190 --> 05:56.080
Do you think people will be less upset 
just because you tell them the truth?

05:56.080 --> 05:56.980
That doesn't mean...

05:56.980 --> 05:58.120
Guys!

05:58.500 --> 05:59.830
They can hear you.

06:08.140 --> 06:09.380
Sorry.

06:09.380 --> 06:11.740
I didn't intend to start an argument.

06:12.390 --> 06:14.810
It'd be bad if you did.

06:16.600 --> 06:19.150
Should we talk to Taki-sensei?

06:19.150 --> 06:23.380
I hate to admit it, but I don't think 
we can handle this on our own anymore.

06:28.510 --> 06:30.110
Kuroe-senpai.

06:31.160 --> 06:33.710
Sectionals are about to start.

06:35.220 --> 06:36.130
Okay.

06:41.210 --> 06:45.210
The classroom wasn't locked, apparently. 
The Kansai Competition is coming up. 
We have to make sure nothing goes wrong. 
-Reina

06:47.180 --> 06:49.350
Then you're a failure of a president.

06:50.830 --> 06:55.850
<i>Reina's comments in the exec 
notes were too normal.</i>

06:56.440 --> 07:00.960
<i>It was like she wanted to 
pretend nothing had happened.</i>

06:58.100 --> 07:01.850
Let's try to get through the Kansai Competition this year.

07:06.360 --> 07:08.860
Sunflower Festival

07:18.500 --> 07:21.330
Mamiko

07:18.500 --> 07:21.330
Reina

07:18.500 --> 07:21.330
Shuichi

07:18.500 --> 07:21.330
Hazuki Midori Kumiko Reina

07:22.370 --> 07:24.960
I'm on my way

07:22.370 --> 07:24.960
I want to talk now

07:22.370 --> 07:24.960
Can we meet at the
 station?

07:22.370 --> 07:24.960
I just arrived at the station

07:30.700 --> 07:32.560
Talk to Taki-sensei?

07:32.560 --> 07:33.050
Yeah.

07:33.830 --> 07:35.660
I think you're right in that

07:35.660 --> 07:41.260
we can't keep playing anymore
unless everyone trusts Taki-sensei.

07:42.050 --> 07:45.440
Then everyone just needs 
to trust Taki-sensei.

07:45.710 --> 07:50.220
I get that, but the first-years 
don't know about the time we got

07:50.220 --> 07:53.030
to the Nationals with a 
miraculous performance.

07:53.030 --> 07:56.150
They can't trust Taki-sensei that much.

07:56.610 --> 07:58.980
But if we keep listening to them...

07:58.980 --> 08:00.670
You're right, Reina.

08:00.670 --> 08:05.550
But this whole problem started 
with Taki-sensei's selection.

08:05.550 --> 08:08.920
If only Taki-sensei would
explain to everyone...

08:10.790 --> 08:12.870
What does the vice principal say?

08:13.450 --> 08:16.380
He agrees in principle.

08:18.600 --> 08:20.520
We want to get gold in the Nationals.

08:21.500 --> 08:26.190
But the way things are now, I don't think we 
can even make it past the Kansai Regionals.

08:26.780 --> 08:27.680
Reina...

08:28.950 --> 08:31.270
I can't agree to this.

08:32.180 --> 08:37.230
The club would be even more messed up if 
Taki-sensei said anything about the auditions.

08:39.190 --> 08:44.320
Anyone who's upset now won't be satisfied 
unless the audition results get changed.

08:44.740 --> 08:49.170
You might be right, but if we just go into 
the Kansai Competition without doing anything...

08:49.170 --> 08:50.370
You aren't doing anything?

08:52.670 --> 08:57.700
Your job as the president is 
to beg Taki-sensei to explain?

08:58.440 --> 09:00.180
To depend on others?

09:00.180 --> 09:01.270
That's not the point!

09:01.270 --> 09:02.510
That's obviously your point!

09:02.510 --> 09:05.390
What do <i>you</i> suggest we do, then?

09:05.390 --> 09:07.840
We wouldn't have a problem 
if all it took was for you

09:07.840 --> 09:09.780
to get up there and tell 
people they're wrong!

09:13.490 --> 09:19.150
It isn't in Kitauji's best interest to 
deviate from what's right for us as performers.

09:19.150 --> 09:20.860
Not now and not ever.

09:31.500 --> 09:38.320
<i>It felt like the line I was desperately 
trying to draw her in with had just snapped.</i>

10:06.040 --> 10:07.110
It's here.

10:13.580 --> 10:14.720
Yes?

10:14.720 --> 10:19.410
Oh, err, is this Asuka Tanaka-san's place?

10:19.410 --> 10:20.270
<i>Yes.</i>

10:20.270 --> 10:21.800
<i>Who might you be?</i>

10:21.800 --> 10:24.810
M-My name is Kumiko Oumae.

10:24.810 --> 10:27.220
<i>Oh, Oumae-san.</i>

10:29.530 --> 10:31.590
Kaori-senpai?

10:31.590 --> 10:32.360
Yeah.

10:32.360 --> 10:34.480
I'm rooming with Asuka.

10:34.480 --> 10:36.010
It saves money.

10:36.010 --> 10:37.680
I had no idea.

10:38.380 --> 10:39.600
Come in.

10:39.600 --> 10:41.730
She should be back soon.

10:41.730 --> 10:43.110
Right.

10:43.990 --> 10:45.360
Are you coming home from rehearsal?

10:45.740 --> 10:46.480
Yes.

10:46.480 --> 10:49.280
The Kansai Competition's 
next Sunday, isn't it?

10:49.580 --> 10:51.100
That takes me back.

10:51.100 --> 10:52.280
Your uniform, too.

10:52.620 --> 10:55.990
Oh, you can turn up the AC if it's too hot.

10:55.990 --> 10:57.400
Oh, no.

11:02.950 --> 11:04.140
What's up?

11:04.460 --> 11:07.360
I've just never seen a shared room before.

11:07.810 --> 11:10.280
There's nothing special about it.

11:10.280 --> 11:13.440
We're just paying rent 
together for the same room.

11:15.060 --> 11:17.460
Did you get in a fight with Kousaka-san?

11:19.150 --> 11:24.740
Asuka said that if you were ever
to use that postcard to come here,

11:24.740 --> 11:27.590
it would be when you got in 
a fight with Kousaka-san.

11:27.590 --> 11:29.150
I see...

11:29.800 --> 11:30.920
Was she right?

11:30.920 --> 11:32.390
Unfortunately.

11:33.050 --> 11:35.430
Well, that's lame.

11:36.600 --> 11:38.110
No kidding.

11:40.680 --> 11:42.250
I'm home.

11:44.470 --> 11:46.300
Is it Oumae-chan?!

11:46.300 --> 11:48.670
Wait, no way! It can't be!

11:49.040 --> 11:50.100
Asuka...

11:50.630 --> 11:51.940
senpai?

11:51.940 --> 11:54.440
You finally had a fight with Kousaka-san?!

11:54.440 --> 11:56.380
Y-You've changed.

11:56.380 --> 11:57.570
Your hair and stuff.

11:57.570 --> 11:59.110
It's nice, right?

11:59.110 --> 12:02.470
I'm thinking of dyeing it purple.

12:02.470 --> 12:03.700
What do you think?

12:06.750 --> 12:08.590
You sure haven't changed.

12:09.440 --> 12:11.440
I see.

12:11.440 --> 12:13.640
A transfer student took the 
audition from you, huh?

12:14.330 --> 12:15.280
Yes.

12:15.850 --> 12:17.460
That's stupid.

12:17.460 --> 12:21.210
I was expecting more of a 
lover's quarrel type of thing.

12:21.480 --> 12:22.390
Lover's quarrel?

12:22.700 --> 12:26.910
"I've decided to go abroad for college."

12:26.910 --> 12:28.590
"Please don't leave me!"

12:28.590 --> 12:29.430
Or something.

12:29.690 --> 12:31.700
What's that supposed to mean?

12:31.700 --> 12:34.180
And the transfer student 
wants to forfeit, huh?

12:34.550 --> 12:36.370
That is pretty complicated.

12:36.850 --> 12:39.120
It's such an easy problem.

12:39.120 --> 12:42.580
Just let her step down and 
play the soli part yourself.

12:42.580 --> 12:46.910
The other sections aside, 
that's all you need to do about her.

12:47.970 --> 12:49.300
Don't be mean.

12:49.780 --> 12:51.520
I'm not being mean.

12:51.520 --> 12:55.330
I'm just being objective 
and logical, aren't I?

12:56.410 --> 12:57.380
But...

12:57.730 --> 12:58.760
But?

12:59.470 --> 13:02.600
But what's the point of an audition, then?

13:02.600 --> 13:04.710
Kitauji is meritocratic.

13:04.710 --> 13:09.010
When you and Reina-senpai auditioned 
on the year I entered...

13:09.910 --> 13:11.190
Go on.

13:11.190 --> 13:12.690
Sorry.

13:12.690 --> 13:17.630
Point is, I can't change that now, after 
we've been doing things that way all this time.

13:16.970 --> 13:18.220
Yeah, yeah.

13:18.220 --> 13:20.180
Thank you for your opinion.

13:20.180 --> 13:22.720
You haven't changed at all, Oumae-chan.

13:23.360 --> 13:29.180
You talk so high-and-mighty, 
but you're really just being selfish.

13:30.240 --> 13:31.570
Selfish?

13:32.000 --> 13:35.420
You want the best person 
in the audition to play.

13:35.420 --> 13:40.230
If you don't get chosen, 
you want Taki-san to explain why.

13:40.230 --> 13:43.910
Either way, you just want closure.

13:43.910 --> 13:45.170
That's...

13:45.170 --> 13:46.600
But you see...

13:47.130 --> 13:51.760
Those aren't necessarily decisions that 
they're making based on clear answers.

13:52.880 --> 13:54.750
What do you mean?

13:55.020 --> 13:59.270
I think Taki-san and that 
kid are both stuck, too.

14:01.390 --> 14:04.640
For there to be so much beef in the club,

14:04.640 --> 14:08.430
there can't be much difference 
in ability between you and her.

14:08.430 --> 14:12.600
So all he can do is to choose one or the 
other and act confident in that decision.

14:14.670 --> 14:18.010
I'm sure Taki-san knows the club's upset,

14:18.010 --> 14:22.190
but he also knows he's screwed 
if he shows hesitation.

14:22.190 --> 14:23.920
That's why he isn't saying anything.

14:24.520 --> 14:25.520
Then...

14:26.020 --> 14:28.460
But what am I supposed to do?

14:28.460 --> 14:31.260
The Kansai Competition is next Sunday!

14:31.260 --> 14:33.050
Not my problem.

14:33.050 --> 14:35.910
But what I like about you

14:35.910 --> 14:39.360
is that you just speak your mind without 
thinking about the consequences.

14:40.080 --> 14:42.200
Like you did to me.

14:42.560 --> 14:47.810
Just so you know, I still don't think you 
were right about a single thing you said.

14:48.970 --> 14:54.210
But I had no choice but to take 
it because you threw a tantrum.

14:54.210 --> 14:55.480
Asuka-senpai?

14:55.920 --> 14:59.960
You never do anything until 
the last moment anyway.

15:00.460 --> 15:02.290
I'm gonna take a shower.

15:04.030 --> 15:05.830
I'm jealous.

15:07.560 --> 15:09.340
You got through to her.

15:15.630 --> 15:16.890
Thank you for having me.

15:17.640 --> 15:18.670
Not at all.

15:20.110 --> 15:24.090
Please tell Asuka-senpai 
that she got through to me.

15:25.140 --> 15:26.100
Okay.

15:26.450 --> 15:28.900
Break a leg, Oumae-san.

15:41.990 --> 15:45.370
Speak my mind.

15:47.380 --> 15:49.760
<b>A lot has happened since camp, but 
I'd never seen you two fight before.</b>

15:47.380 --> 15:53.450
<i>A lot has happened since camp, but 
I'd never seen you two fight before.</i>

15:54.320 --> 15:59.150
<i>And I realized I should have 
confronted you properly.</i>

16:00.820 --> 16:05.600
<i>To be honest, I'm not entirely satisfied 
with Taki-sensei's choices.</i>

16:05.990 --> 16:08.570
<i>I can relate to the discontent in the club.</i>

16:08.570 --> 16:10.620
<i>That's why I couldn't say anything.</i>

16:08.570 --> 16:10.820
Exec Note

16:10.620 --> 16:13.270
<i>But I want all of us to 
perform well together.</i>

16:13.270 --> 16:16.480
<i>And I want us to be glad we did.</i>

16:17.070 --> 16:22.690
<i>I'm confident Taki-sensei and all the 
club members feel the same about that.</i>

16:23.960 --> 16:24.970
<i>Which is why...</i>

16:26.080 --> 16:27.760
<i>Even though it's right before</i>

16:27.760 --> 16:30.330
<i>our performance, I'm going
to talk to everyone about it.</i>

16:31.040 --> 16:33.830
<i>I'm going to say what I think.</i>

16:34.940 --> 16:36.220
I'm going...

16:37.980 --> 16:39.520
To put my thoughts to words.

16:43.520 --> 16:46.840
And tell them everything.

17:03.010 --> 17:06.490
I'm telling everyone.

17:06.750 --> 17:11.260
I'll have your back if it looks
 like you're about to botch it, Kumiko 
-Shuichi

17:06.750 --> 17:11.260
For the first time, I agree 
-Reina

17:38.280 --> 17:40.660
Yup, brass over there.

17:41.020 --> 17:43.030
Be on time, everyone.

17:43.440 --> 17:44.600
Find it?

17:44.600 --> 17:46.550
Yeah, they found it.

17:46.540 --> 17:49.040
Greenroom

17:47.070 --> 17:49.040
Horns present.

17:49.330 --> 17:51.030
Bass present.

17:51.390 --> 17:53.000
All present.

17:53.000 --> 17:53.800
Okay.

17:53.800 --> 17:56.630
Let's move to the tuning room.

17:57.670 --> 18:00.540
Kanade, I'm counting on you.

18:02.800 --> 18:03.700
Hey!

18:03.700 --> 18:04.690
Sorry!

18:04.690 --> 18:05.960
I just...

18:05.960 --> 18:07.420
Are we going to be all right?

18:10.200 --> 18:12.400
I'm going to do my best on the soli.

18:13.830 --> 18:19.490
After all, you won't have a chance to play 
it if we don't make it past this.

18:25.050 --> 18:27.680
Am I in tune? Am I in tune?

18:27.680 --> 18:28.830
You're fine.

18:28.830 --> 18:30.430
Relax.

18:30.430 --> 18:31.600
From the top.

18:31.600 --> 18:33.600
One last time, please.

19:03.160 --> 19:05.140
Okay, that's enough.

19:05.940 --> 19:07.300
Excellent.

19:07.300 --> 19:08.790
You sound great.

19:09.070 --> 19:10.840
How much longer?

19:10.840 --> 19:12.300
About ten more minutes.

19:13.200 --> 19:20.000
I believe that Kitauji's music, 
your music, is fantastic.

19:20.540 --> 19:22.300
I'm sure you'll be thinking 
about the results,

19:22.300 --> 19:26.050
but let's make it a performance 
that we can be proud of.

19:26.050 --> 19:27.300
Yes.

19:27.300 --> 19:28.360
Hi...

19:28.800 --> 19:30.560
May I say something?

19:34.660 --> 19:35.930
Of course.

19:39.500 --> 19:41.130
I'm Oumae, the president.

19:42.450 --> 19:43.950
Um...

19:44.800 --> 19:46.950
<i>Stay calm. Stay calm.</i>

19:48.080 --> 19:49.690
<i>Say what you're thinking.</i>

19:50.390 --> 19:52.000
Just say it.

19:52.000 --> 19:53.700
Don't overthink it.

19:53.930 --> 19:55.270
It'll be okay.

19:55.270 --> 19:56.690
Slowly.

19:58.170 --> 20:01.850
Say what you're thinking.

20:00.230 --> 20:01.500
Kumiko!

20:05.010 --> 20:09.440
Sorry, I have a habit of blurting 
out what's on my mind.

20:10.190 --> 20:12.050
So, um...

20:13.550 --> 20:15.550
I'm going to say what I'm thinking.

20:15.550 --> 20:16.900
Honestly.

20:16.900 --> 20:17.990
No filter.

20:23.190 --> 20:31.060
At Kitauji, the first-years and 
third-years can compete in the same ring.

20:31.060 --> 20:32.450
For that, I love it.

20:32.450 --> 20:35.450
And I want for us, Kitauji, 
to get gold in the Nationals.

20:35.760 --> 20:37.970
I've wanted that for two years.

20:38.420 --> 20:41.590
But we never made it.

20:42.300 --> 20:47.670
The second-years, third-years, and 
Taki-sensei, must all be thinking the same.

20:48.430 --> 20:50.040
Why, dammit?

20:51.100 --> 20:55.410
Which is why, as the executives, 
we decided we needed to change something,

20:55.410 --> 20:58.360
and proposed the audition format this year.

20:58.880 --> 21:01.570
I don't think we were wrong about it.

21:01.970 --> 21:04.990
I also think it's a decision 
befitting of Kitauji.

21:05.370 --> 21:09.740
But it's true that some were 
apprehensive about it.

21:09.740 --> 21:12.790
As the president, I'd like 
to apologize for that.

21:13.730 --> 21:15.510
I'm sorry.

21:15.510 --> 21:16.620
Kumiko...

21:24.220 --> 21:28.820
I'm sure not all of you can 
accept such a belated apology.

21:29.930 --> 21:30.690
But...

21:31.690 --> 21:35.520
But still, I want to win gold with Kitauji.

21:36.550 --> 21:38.220
Maybe that's selfish.

21:38.220 --> 21:41.150
I want those of us here to put 
on the best performance ever

21:41.150 --> 21:46.220
so we can blow away all the discontent and 
hesitation and make it to the Nationals.

21:47.480 --> 21:51.230
After a year of watching us, I realized...

21:51.540 --> 21:55.190
There's no way we haven't gotten 
good after we practiced so much.

21:55.570 --> 21:59.160
There's no way we wouldn't get through 
to people with how much we put into it.

21:59.620 --> 22:01.330
Kitauji can do it!

22:01.730 --> 22:03.660
We can do it!

22:03.660 --> 22:05.680
So have confidence!

22:05.680 --> 22:08.370
Have faith in what we've done!

22:08.850 --> 22:11.610
So... Umm...

22:11.610 --> 22:13.650
What I'm trying to say is...

22:18.600 --> 22:21.110
I want to go to the Nationals, too!

22:21.110 --> 22:22.730
Me, too!

22:23.010 --> 22:26.110
I want the National gold, too!

22:26.620 --> 22:29.190
Let's go to the Nationals!

22:39.180 --> 22:40.220
Kumiko.

22:43.870 --> 22:45.980
All right, let's do a cheer.

22:46.690 --> 22:51.920
Go, Kitauji!

24:49.960 --> 24:53.870
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

24:52.050 --> 24:56.010
<b>To be continued</b>
